From 8566e2cd5d8da0871ffda4b1c99028907099dd28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:11:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cli): hide and retire agent-started proof chats [daveey]

Problem: agent-started interactive CLI proof chats appeared in human session lists.
Why 1: CLI source labels describe surface, not authorship.
Why 2: start-time agent ancestry (including forwarded LC_HERMES_AGENT) was
already detected for comment attribution but not consulted on session create.
Why 3: canonical hidden was applied after commit and excluded from create
receipt identity, so creation did not have one durable visibility contract.
Root (happened): CLI authorship was not propagated across the create boundary.
Root (not caught): ancestry and row creation were tested separately, without
a marked-process create-to-row regression or independent retirement coverage.
Recurrence: websocket agent clients were already hidden; CLI callers were not.

Countermeasures:
- Classify start-time ancestry, not main's own advertised runtime environment.
- Freeze hidden/agent_cli in create receipts; set hidden atomically with the row.
- Retain CLI surface and all owner/terminal authorization gates.
- --visible / HERMES_CHAT_VISIBLE=1 explicitly preserve sidebar visibility.
- Archive ended/done proofs or 24h-idle proofs independently of auto_archive.
- Leave human, manually hidden, and explicitly visible chats untouched.

Proof: focused ancestry, real parent-environment subprocess, create/retry and
retirement tests pass. Initial new create test failed invalid_params on
params.agent_cli; CLI tests failed missing hidden and unknown --visible;
retirement tests failed to archive ended and idle proof rows before the fix.

